CLI COMMANDS VERIFIED
---------------------
- run --capability <name> [--input <json>]: execute task
- run --capability <nope>: not found -> EXIT_NOT_FOUND
- task <id>: look up task -> EXIT_NOT_FOUND if missing
- run "rm -rf /": safety block -> EXIT_NOT_FOUND
- cancel <task_id>: cancel task -> EXIT_FAILURE if terminal
- permissions: show permissions -> EXIT_OK
- retry <task_id>: retry task -> EXIT_UNSAFE if not retry-safe
- --json <subcommand>: JSON output for any subcommand
- --quiet: minimal output mode
- summary --rebuild: rebuild summary -> EXIT_OK
- summary --verify: verify summary -> EXIT_OK

EXIT CODE MAP (full)
--------------------
0: EXIT_OK - successful completion
1: EXIT_NOT_FOUND - task/capability not found
2: EXIT_FAILURE - operation refused (terminal, unsafe)
3: EXIT_RECOVERY_REQUIRED - capability not replay-safe
4: EXIT_CANCELLED - task was cancelled
5: EXIT_CONFIG - configuration invalid
6: EXIT_UNSAFE - retry of non-retry-safe capability

--json: produces valid JSON dict output for any subcommand
--quiet: minimal one-line output
--verbose: (global flag, detailed logging)